:2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It keeps a copy of the graph to look vertices up through the graph’s own vertex indices, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"component(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" hashes nothing on a graph whose indices are its vertices. The copy shares"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"storage (copy-on-write), so making it is O(1), and later changes to the original do not affect"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the result. The cost comes later: while the result is alive, the next mutation of the original"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"copies the whole graph, as it would with any other copy. Drop the result, or keep only what"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"you need from it ("},{"code":"Array(components)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), before mutating the graph."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A component’s slice keeps the indices of the flat storage it is cut from, as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"CompressedSparseRow.successors(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" does: use ","type":"text"},{"code":"first","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", iteration or ","type":"text"},{"code":"Array(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", not ","type":"text"},{"code":"[0]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Because its type names the graph’s type, a result cannot be returned through an existential","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"any DirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": call it from a generic function (","type":"text"},{"code":"some DirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") instead.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/connectivity\/components"]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"re